  "term": "strabismus",
  "definition": "Strabismus is a condition in which the eyes are not aligned so they do not point in the same direction. In some forms the amount of misalignment stays the same in different directions of gaze, while in others it changes depending on where the person looks or which eye is focusing on the target.",
